{"study_accession":"PRJNA763564","secondary_study_accession":"SRP337247","title":"RNA-seq from CD4 T lymphocytes of cirrhotic patients with cognitive impairment","description":"Patients with liver cirrhosis may have minimal hepatic encephalopathy (MHE) with cognitive and motor impairments that reduce life quality and span. MHE onset is associated with a shift in peripheral inflammation in which CD4+ lymphocytes play a key role but the underlying mechanisms remain unclear. We aimed to identify in CD4+ lymphocytes from patients with and without MHE: (1) gene expression changes and associated biological pathways using RNA-seq; (2) alterations in miRNA levels using miRNA-seq; (3) miRNAs and transcription factors regulating key mRNAs and (4) signalling pathways contributing to the peripheral inflammation shift associated to MHE onset. Additionally, we recovered T-cell receptor (TCR) repertoires from RNA-seq dataset to understand the immune status of control patients and cirrhotic patients with or without MHE. Overall design: Gene expression was measured using RNA-seq in CD4 T cells of control and cirrhotic patients with and without minimal hepatic encephalopathy.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":20,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN21442589","study_accession":"PRJNA763564","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"RNA-Seq CD4_control_CR219","description":"RNA-Seq CD4_control_CR219","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM5580179","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-04-04","attributes":[["source_name","CD4 T-cell, control"],["cell_type","Peripheral CD4 T-cells"],["disease","control"],["age","65"],["sex","male"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR15905015","experiment_accession":"SRX12195463","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":71853953,"base_count":17963488250,"first_public":"2022-04-04","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM5580179: